d to adolescent health issues, including eating disorders. The Society for Adolescent Health and Medicine's involvement with this journal highlights the importance of disseminating knowledge and research findings to improve clinical practices and health outcomes for adolescents [Data: Entities (8974); Relationships (17344)].", "# Nutritional Support Community in El Ejido\n\nThe community is centered around key medical professionals specializing in nutritional support for patients with chronic conditions, particularly renal and liver diseases. Dr. Juan Pedro Rodríguez Rodríguez serves as a pivotal figure, connected to various other specialists and the Hospital de Poniente, highlighting a collaborative network focused on improving patient outcomes.\n\n## Dr. Juan Pedro Rodríguez Rodríguez as a central figure\n\nDr. Juan Pedro Rodríguez Rodríguez is a resident in internal medicine at Hospital de Poniente and specializes in nutritional support for patients with chronic conditions. His focus on renal patients and those with chronic liver disease positions him as a key player in this community. His work emphasizes tailored nutritional interventions, which are crucial for improving health outcomes in these vulnerable populations. The relationships he maintains with other medical professionals further enhance the collaborative nature of this community, allowing for a comprehensive approach to patient care. [Data: Entities (10047, 10061); Relationships (18076, 18077)]\n\n## Collaboration among specialists\n\nThe community consists of several medical professionals, including Dr. Luis Miguel Luengo, Dr. Pedro Pablo García Luna, and Dra. Mercedes Vázquez Gutiérrez, who all focus on nutritional support for patients with renal and liver conditions. This collaboration is vital as it allows for shared knowledge and resources, ultimately benefiting patient care. The interconnectedness of these professionals through various relationships indicates a strong network dedicated to addres