; Relationships (20576)]\n\n## Interconnectedness of entities in clinical trial regulation\n\nThe relationships among the key entities in this community illustrate a complex network of regulatory oversight and ethical compliance. Real Decreto 1090/2015 connects with various entities, including ethical committees, data protection laws, and the clinical studies registry, creating a comprehensive framework for clinical trial governance. This interconnectedness is vital for ensuring that all aspects of clinical research are addressed, from ethical considerations to data privacy and public transparency. The collaborative nature of these relationships underscores the importance of a cohesive regulatory environment in safeguarding public health. [Data: Relationships (2597, 17261, 20573, 20575, 20576)]", "# Clinical Trials and Gastrointestinal Disorders\n\nThis community focuses on the interrelated entities of clinical trials, gastrointestinal disorders such as Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) and gluten sensitivity, and the ethical frameworks governing medical research. The relationships among these entities highlight the importance of clinical trials in evaluating treatments for these conditions, as well as the legal and ethical considerations involved.\n\n## Importance of Clinical Trials\n\nClinical trials are essential for evaluating the safety and efficacy of new treatments, particularly for conditions like IBS and gluten sensitivity. These trials provide the necessary data to inform medical practices and improve patient outcomes. The rigorous testing involved in clinical trials ensures that new therapies are both effective and safe for public use. This is particularly relevant in the context of gastrointestinal disorders, where treatment options are often limited and require thorough investigation to validate their effectiveness. [Data: Entities (8651), Relationships (835, 15867, 17259)]\n\n## Connection between IBS and Gluten Sensitivity\n\nIrritable Bowel Syndrome and